---
description: React/TypeScript HADES UI rules
globs:
  - "components/**/*.tsx"
  - "components/**/*.ts"
  - "lib/**/*.ts"
  - "main.tsx"
  - "app/**/*.css"
alwaysApply: false
---
- Preserve the established HADES visual language and navigation unless redesign is explicitly requested.
- Use `lib/hades-api.ts` as the frontend API contract rather than duplicating fetch logic in pages.
- UI success state must reflect confirmed backend state, not optimistic assumptions for service/plugin lifecycle actions.
- Keep pages responsive during long operations; show actionable errors and persisted status where available.
- Maintain accessibility semantics on interactive controls.
- Typecheck after API/type changes and build after CSS/import changes.
